  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Library of Ahmed III/Enderun Library: mapped cross-shaped marble building, raised basement and paired side stairs, open three-bay pointed-arch portico/four pale shafts, real central doorway, two recessed window rows with metal grilles, main lead dome on octagonal drum, three small portico domes, low barrel roofs over three arms and front fountain. No copied inscriptions, floral carving, visitors, planting or furnished library.",
    "identityBasis": "Independent Library Q104549762, within Topkapi Q170495, OSM way32396231/native35184404485063. Existing parent has twelve cross-plan corners and two detailed tile fragments. Internal+X follows front elevation southeast; internal+Z faces southwest toward separate Audience Chamber. World heading0/+X east/+Z south. Ordinary photos show the same front portico, raised basement, window rows and lead roofs.",
    "heightBasis": "No qualified native height. Picture-led floor2.2m above open front court, main eaves10.9m, portico arch spring8.3m/crown10.45m, central octagonal drum12.0m and lead dome14.9m plus finial. Three portico domes and shallow arm vaults follow photos; heights/profiles, exact hidden roof joins, room layout and fine decoration remain approximate.",
    "terrainBasis": "Source vertical datum remains 51.31288038632903m, preserving authored geometry and its native position. Actual provider attachment uses the uncovered front gap internal[0,9.6], outside every one of the 573 retained native building records, with modelHeight=-0.29670710644687404m. This negative local attachment height compensates for the original grid slope. Original terrain/roads/water remain unchanged; occupied floorY2.2 and deep rear/east foundations are approximate accommodations, not verified historical basement heights. No precinct flattening/custom terrain; thresholds/accessibility remain unverified.",
